    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p024:u012.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-024">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:collects_logs_from" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-siem" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-management" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The association records the source configuration without asserting deployment or a property restriction.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source assigns collection and analysis of the named target logs to the Gray SIEM.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p024:u012.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-025">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:supports" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-cds" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-red-siem" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The source permits the Red-side alternative under the stated approval and annex conditions.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>An approved CDS can move Gray Network log data to a Red SIEM.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u001.s003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p030:u003.s003" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-026">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:comprises" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-red-management" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-management-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Composition is recorded as an annotation. The aggregate is not made a subclass of its constituent Management component category.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source describes Red Management Services as an aggregate of components.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u011.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-027">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:comprises" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-management" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-management-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Composition is recorded as an annotation. The aggregate is not made a subclass of its constituent Management component category.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source describes Gray Management Services as an aggregate of components.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p024:u008.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-028">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:supports_certificate_provisioning" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-inner-ca" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-inner-vpn" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The relation records the certificate-based provisioning passage. No CA administration or device identity is inferred.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The Security Administrator delivers the inner gateway CSR to the corresponding CA, which returns a signed certificate.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s002" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s004" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-029">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:supports_certificate_provisioning" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-ca" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-vpn" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The relation records the certificate-based provisioning passage. No CA administration or device identity is inferred.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The Security Administrator delivers the outer gateway CSR to the corresponding CA, which returns a signed certificate.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s002" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s004" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-030">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:provides_revocation_information_to" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-cdp" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-vpn-gateway" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The relation describes the CDP function. No location or deployment cardinality is asserted.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The CDP hosts a CRL issued by a CA for VPN Gateways to download.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u001.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="association-031">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:supports" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-registration-authority" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-ca" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The RA can comprise hardware, software, and personnel. The annotation does not type the RA as a physical device or equate it with the certificate registration component.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The RA collects, verifies, and submits certificate information under CA authorization.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p061:u005.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p061:u005.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-001">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-encryption-component" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-solution-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>Section 5 presents the encryption components as components of the MSC Solution. The edge applies to the source-context Encryption Component category.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p022:u003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p022:u004.s002" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p022:u005.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-002">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-vpn-gateway" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-encryption-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The glossary defines an Encryption Component as either a VPN Gateway or a MACsec Device. Each named alternative is included under the defined category.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u004.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-003">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-macsec-device" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-encryption-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The glossary includes MACsec Devices in the Encryption Component category.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u004.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-004">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-inner-encryption" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-encryption-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>Inner Encryption Components use the VPN Gateway or MACsec Device alternatives that define an Encryption Component.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u003.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u004.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-005">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-encryption" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-encryption-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>Outer Encryption Components use the VPN Gateway or MACsec Device alternatives that define an Encryption Component.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p023:u007.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u004.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-006">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-inner-vpn" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-vpn-gateway" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The provisioning text names Inner VPN Gateways as the inner specialization of VPN Gateways.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-007">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-inner-vpn" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-inner-encryption" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The Inner Encryption Component requirements identify the Inner VPN Gateway as their VPN realization.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p042:u016.s002" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p042:u018" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-008">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-vpn" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-vpn-gateway" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The provisioning text names Outer VPN Gateways as the outer specialization of VPN Gateways.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-009">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-vpn" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-encryption" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The Outer Encryption Component requirements identify Outer VPN Gateways as their VPN realization.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p043:u010.s002" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p043:u012" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-010">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-inner-macsec" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-macsec-device" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The source names an Inner MACsec Device as the inner specialization of a MACsec Device.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u007.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-011">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-inner-macsec" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-inner-encryption" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>Section 5.5 identifies MACsec Devices as an Inner Encryption Component realization and then describes the Inner MACsec Device.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u003.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u007.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-012">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-macsec" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-macsec-device" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>MSC-PF-4 names the Outer MACsec Device specialization.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p044:u017" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-013">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-macsec" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-encryption" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The outer component can be a MACsec Device; MSC-PF-4 names the Outer MACsec Device and its Black Network interfaces.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p023:u007.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p044:u017" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-014">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-firewall" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-firewall" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The source names the firewall at the outer edge as the Outer Firewall.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p023:u001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p023:u002.s004" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-015">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-firewall" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-firewall" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The glossary explicitly defines a Gray Firewall as a traffic filtering firewall.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u009.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-016">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-inner-firewall" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-firewall" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The edge does not make an Inner Firewall mandatory. Requirements can come from another CP.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>Section 5.6 names the firewall between the Inner Encryption Component and Red Network as the Inner Firewall.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u008" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u009.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-017">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-firewall" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-solution-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Membership does not imply presence in every MSC deployment.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source describes individual solution components and identifies the Outer Firewall as an exception to their physical-protection requirement.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p022:u006.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p022:u006.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-018">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-firewall" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-solution-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The source makes Gray Firewall deployment depend on the network design. The subtype axiom expresses category membership only.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>Section 5 includes Gray Firewalls among the solution components.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p022:u004.s003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p022:u005.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-019">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-aw" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-management-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The superclass is the generic extracted Management component category. No universal Solution Component membership follows.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The administration section describes AWs as the components whose combined management functions satisfy the administrative requirements.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p030:u003.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p030:u003.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-020">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-red-aw" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-aw" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The Red AW is the named Red-side specialization of the Administrative Workstation.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u002.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-021">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-aw" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-aw" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The Gray Administrative Workstation subsection defines the Gray AW specialization.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p024:u009" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p024:u010.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-022">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-black-aw" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-aw" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The subtype axiom does not authorize Black AW management of Gray components or place Black AWs inside the MSC Solution.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The prohibition names Black AWs alongside Red AWs, supporting the workstation specialization without supplying a positive MSC assignment.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p011:u009.s006" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-023">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-red-aw" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-solution-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The source includes AWs among solution components and requires at least one Red AW in every MSC Solution.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p022:u004.s003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u002.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u002.s003" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-024">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-aw" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-solution-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The source includes AWs among solution components and requires at least one Gray AW in every MSC Solution.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p022:u004.s003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p024:u010.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p024:u010.s003" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-025">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-red-siem" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-siem" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>Section 5.7.2 identifies the Red SIEM specialization of Security Information and Event Management.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u004.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-026">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-siem" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-siem" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>Gray SIEM membership does not make a Gray SIEM mandatory.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>Section 5.4.2 identifies the Gray SIEM specialization of Security Information and Event Management.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p024:u011" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p024:u012.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-027">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-inner-ca" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-ca" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The provisioning text names the CA receiving Inner VPN Gateway certificate signing requests as the Inner CA.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-028">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-ca" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-ca" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The provisioning text names the CA receiving Outer VPN Gateway certificate signing requests as the Outer CA.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-029">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-local-ca" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-ca" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The ontology does not declare local and enterprise CAs disjoint.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source explicitly presents locally run CAs as one CA option.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p014:u006.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-030">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-enterprise-ca" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-ca" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The source says enterprise CAs are not necessarily managed by the Solution Owner. No Solution Component subclass is asserted for the generic CA category.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source explicitly presents enterprise CAs as another CA option.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p014:u006.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-031">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-root-ca" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-ca" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The example does not establish Root CA and Trust Anchor CA equivalence or a universal subclass relationship between them.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The certificate-chain example names a Root CA certificate, preserving Root CA as a CA specialization.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s005" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s006" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s007" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-032">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-signing-ca" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-ca" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>The certificate-chain passage names the signing CA as the authority whose certificate appears in the chain.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p029:u011.s005" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-033">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-trust-anchor-ca" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-ca" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>MSC-VG-4 names the Trust Anchor CA certificate within the corresponding CA certificate chain.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p038:u009" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-034">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-key-server" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-macsec-device" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The class denotes a MACsec Device bearing the designated key-server role. No assertion makes every MACsec Device a Key Server.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The glossary defines a Key Server as the MACsec Device designated to distribute Secure Association Keys.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u013.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-035">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-router" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-router" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The edge does not impose general Solution Component requirements on the Gray Network router.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The availability example identifies an ordinary router on each Gray Network as the device that selects an outer component.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p021:u008.s003" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-036">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-screening-router" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-router" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The source excludes the screening router from the MSC Solution itself.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source describes a screening router as a router used to filter packets from Black Networks.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u010.s002" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-037">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-customer-edge-router" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-router" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The example does not make all Customer Edge Routers Screening Routers.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The source names a Customer Edge Router as an existing Black Network router that can provide the screening realization.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u010.s003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u010.s004" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u010.s005" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-038">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-authentication-server" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-solution-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_stated</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:rationale>MSC-SR-24 lists Authentication Servers among solution components. The extracted category is the MSC Authentication Server described in Section 5.8.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p037:u003" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-039">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-kgs" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-solution-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The edge identifies the KGS category in the source solution. It does not require the pre-shared-key option in every deployment.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>Section 5 includes a KGS among solution components for generating pre-shared CAKs.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p022:u004.s003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p022:u005.s001" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-040">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-key-management-component" />
    <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-management-component" />
    <tdn:basis>source_interpretation</tdn:basis>
    <tdn:qualification>The heading supplies the category, while detailed requirements are relocated to annexes. No device realization or CA membership follows from the heading alone.</tdn:qualification>
    <tdn:rationale>The named Key and Certificate Management Components category specializes the extracted generic Management component category.</tdn:rationale>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u007" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="subclass-041">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" />
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" />
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-solution-component" />
