  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology" />
    <rdfs:comment>A class describes entities matching an extracted role or realization concept. Classes may overlap and may have multiple parents. No device existence, class disjointness, or class equivalence is asserted. Non-subtype links are OWL annotation assertions between class IRIs. They preserve source context without imposing object-property restrictions or asserting a relationship for every class member.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:versionInfo>CSfC MSC 1.3.0; TDN role hierarchy 1.1; TDN theory v3.2</owl:versionInfo>
    <tdn:inputHash>TDN/Requirements/CoreMscRequirements.lean sha256:a9cdac1d350b6a58f3179db46a5f94cec07e6ae439bfa439b88ed73b46781d60</tdn:inputHash>
    <tdn:inputHash>TDN/Requirements/CrossEnclavePkiIsolationSpec.lean sha256:b2215ad3fe0f334437be321a31f1ea89735fc03772386001d8cee57532410b9d</tdn:inputHash>
