  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-cdp">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:comment>Web server hosting a CRL for VPN Gateways to download.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>CRL Distribution Point</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ExtractedRole" />
    <skos:altLabel>CDP</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>CDPs</skos:altLabel>
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-013" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-020" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-039" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-040" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-067" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-013" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-020" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-039" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-040" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-067" />
    <tdn:leanExpression>DeviceKind.revocationService</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanExpression>ManagementServiceFunction.revocation</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanMapping>Both roles are represented through the broader revocationService kind and revocation service information. DeviceKind does not distinguish CDP from OCSP responders.</tdn:leanMapping>
    <tdn:leanReference>DeviceKind at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:11</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>ManagementServiceFunction at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:554</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>msc_gray_firewall_path_coverage at TDN/Requirements/MasterMscRequirementSpecs.lean:20</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanRepresentation>context</tdn:leanRepresentation>
    <tdn:provides_revocation_information_to rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-vpn-gateway" />
    <tdn:roleId>ROLE-cdp</tdn:roleId>
    <tdn:roleKind>device_or_service_role</tdn:roleKind>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p035:u010" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p045:u013" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p046:u012" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u001.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p062:u013" />
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-013: The Gray path specification distinguishes Inner components, Gray Firewalls, workstations, locally run CAs, all CAs and revocation services. Gray AWs and locally run CAs follow the highest-level convention. The broader service-path requirements retain each service’s actual level.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-cds">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:comment>Controlled interface across security domains, including transfer of Gray logs to a Red SIEM.</rdfs:comment>
