    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u012.s003" />
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-007: V3.1 separates encryption mechanism, Inner/Outer layer, interface zone and full security level. Flow.Valid binds the two tunnel endpoints and independent key contexts. AuthenticationServices requires a CA or key-generation service according to each component’s selected authentication method. Workstations are optional under the current scope.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31R-033: Mandatory MTU bounds include Inner Gray interfaces, Outer Black interfaces and applicable Gray Firewall external interfaces. The separate Inner fragmentation-reduction objective remains optional.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-end-user-device">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:comment>Device category in combined CSfC solutions referenced by MSC-SR-13.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>End user device</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ExtractedRole" />
    <skos:altLabel>end user devices</skos:altLabel>
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-008" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-055" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-056" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-008" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-055" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-056" />
    <tdn:leanExpression>RedNetworkIdentity</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanMapping>Red network records and modeled payload origins identify source and destination networks. DeviceKind has no separate end-user-host constructor.</tdn:leanMapping>
    <tdn:leanReference>RedNetworkIdentity at TDN/Requirements/TwoLayerOverlayArchitecture.lean:13</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanRepresentation>context</tdn:leanRepresentation>
    <tdn:roleId>ROLE-end-user-device</tdn:roleId>
    <tdn:roleKind>device_or_service_role</tdn:roleKind>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p036:u003" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-enrollment-server">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:comment>Enrollment function mentioned in restrictions on cohosting management functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Enrollment server</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ExtractedRole" />
    <skos:altLabel>enrollment or provisioning servers</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>enrollment,</skos:altLabel>
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-048" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-048" />
    <tdn:leanMapping>V3.1 does not define a separate role or protocol model for this certificate-provisioning function.</tdn:leanMapping>
    <tdn:leanRepresentation>unrepresented</tdn:leanRepresentation>
    <tdn:roleId>ROLE-enrollment-server</tdn:roleId>
    <tdn:roleKind>device_or_service_role</tdn:roleKind>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p030:u004.s002" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p030:u004.s004" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p049:u012" />
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-enterprise-ca">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:comment>Enterprise CA that need not be managed by the Solution Owner.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Enterprise CA</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-ca" />
    <skos:altLabel>enterprise CAs</skos:altLabel>
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-007" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-011" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-017" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-020" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-024" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-048" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-067" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-011" />
    <tdn:inheritedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-007" />
    <tdn:inheritedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-017" />
    <tdn:inheritedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-020" />
    <tdn:inheritedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-024" />
    <tdn:inheritedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-048" />
    <tdn:inheritedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-067" />
    <tdn:leanExpression>DeviceKind.certificationAuthority</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanMapping>Enterprise CAs can be listed as CA devices and Gray service nodes. V3.1 does not give enterprise CAs a distinct DeviceKind.</tdn:leanMapping>
    <tdn:leanReference>DeviceKind at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:11</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>msc_gray_firewall_path_coverage at TDN/Requirements/MasterMscRequirementSpecs.lean:20</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanRepresentation>context</tdn:leanRepresentation>
    <tdn:roleId>ROLE-enterprise-ca</tdn:roleId>
    <tdn:roleKind>device_or_service_role</tdn:roleKind>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p014:u006.s002" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p015:u002.s004" />
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-013: The Gray path specification distinguishes Inner components, Gray Firewalls, workstations, locally run CAs, all CAs and revocation services. Gray AWs and locally run CAs follow the highest-level convention. The broader service-path requirements retain each service’s actual level.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
  </rdf:Description>
