    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-012: Credential separation applies to the selected certificate or shared-key method. Management-device presence and separation are required only when managementSelected is true. Different network names do not imply different full security levels.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-013: The Gray path specification distinguishes Inner components, Gray Firewalls, workstations, locally run CAs, all CAs and revocation services. Gray AWs and locally run CAs follow the highest-level convention. The broader service-path requirements retain each service’s actual level.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-router">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:comment>Selects a redundant Outer Encryption Component in the availability example.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Gray Network router</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-router" />
    <skos:altLabel>ordinary router</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>router/switch</skos:altLabel>
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-075" />
    <tdn:inheritedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-075" />
    <tdn:leanExpression>Deployment.OrdinaryGray</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanExpression>Device.kind = .ordinaryGrayRouter</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanMapping>An ordinary Gray router has the router kind, no encryption layer and no infrastructure flag. It has at least one Gray interface; every other interface is Gray or local. Local includes device-internal interfaces such as loopback.</tdn:leanMapping>
    <tdn:leanReference>Deployment.OrdinaryGray at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:668</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>DeviceKind at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:11</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>Zone at TDN/Requirements/TwoLayerOverlayArchitecture.lean:40</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanRepresentation>composed</tdn:leanRepresentation>
    <tdn:roleId>ROLE-gray-router</tdn:roleId>
    <tdn:roleKind>device_or_service_role</tdn:roleKind>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p021:u008.s003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p021:u008.s004" />
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-056-074: Ordinary Gray routing and switching infrastructure has a narrowly defined exemption from component duties. OrdinaryGray requires the matching kind, no encryption layer or infrastructure flag, at least one Gray interface, and only Gray or local interfaces. Standalone encapsulators retain their applicable duties.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-siem">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:comment>Collects Gray-side logs; explicitly not a mandatory component.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Gray SIEM</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-siem" />
    <skos:altLabel>GRAY SECURITY INFORMATION AND EVENT MANAGEMENT</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Gray Security Information and Event Management</skos:altLabel>
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-050" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-062" />
    <tdn:collects_logs_from rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-firewall" />
    <tdn:collects_logs_from rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-gray-management" />
    <tdn:collects_logs_from rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-outer-encryption" />
    <tdn:inheritedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-050" />
    <tdn:inheritedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-062" />
    <tdn:leanExpression>Device.kind = .siem</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanExpression>Interface.zone = .gray</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanMapping>The SIEM kind combines with a Gray interface or management-service domain. The zone is recorded separately from the device kind.</tdn:leanMapping>
    <tdn:leanReference>DeviceKind at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:11</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>Interface at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:26</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>ManagementServiceInstance at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:567</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanRepresentation>composed</tdn:leanRepresentation>
    <tdn:roleId>ROLE-gray-siem</tdn:roleId>
    <tdn:roleKind>device_or_service_role</tdn:roleKind>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p004:u024" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p024:u011" />
