    <tdn:leanExpression>GrayTopology.localCA</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanMapping>The CA kind and its placement can be recorded. GrayTopology separately lists locally run CA nodes for the selected Gray management security-level convention.</tdn:leanMapping>
    <tdn:leanReference>DeviceKind at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:11</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>msc_gray_firewall_path_coverage at TDN/Requirements/MasterMscRequirementSpecs.lean:20</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanRepresentation>context</tdn:leanRepresentation>
    <tdn:roleId>ROLE-local-ca</tdn:roleId>
    <tdn:roleKind>device_or_service_role</tdn:roleKind>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p014:u006.s002" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p018:u001.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p018:u001.s002" />
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-013: The Gray path specification distinguishes Inner components, Gray Firewalls, workstations, locally run CAs, all CAs and revocation services. Gray AWs and locally run CAs follow the highest-level convention. The broader service-path requirements retain each service’s actual level.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-locally-managed-device">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:comment>Management-mode role defined by a hardwired AW connection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Locally Managed Device</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ExtractedRole" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-044" />
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-046" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-044" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-046" />
    <tdn:leanExpression>AdministrativeSession</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanExpression>ManagementExchange</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanMapping>Administrative operation and connection records describe management access. V3.1 does not divide devices into local-management and remote-management kinds.</tdn:leanMapping>
    <tdn:leanReference>AdministrativeAccount at TDN/Requirements/ManagementPlaneRequirements.lean:20</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>ManagementExchange at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:547</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>msc_administrator_authentication at TDN/Requirements/MasterMscRequirementSpecs.lean:94</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanRepresentation>context</tdn:leanRepresentation>
    <tdn:roleId>ROLE-locally-managed-device</tdn:roleId>
    <tdn:roleKind>management_or_realization_facet</tdn:roleKind>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u014.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p061:u006.s001" />
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-047: Administrative Workstations are optional. When deployed, administrator accounts and active sessions must bind each accepted operation to the appropriate individual and prior authentication. Certificate and NIST objectives add their selected assurance conditions.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-log-repository">
