    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p041:u016" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p042:u003" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p042:u004" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p042:u005" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p042:u007" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p042:u010" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p042:u011" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p042:u012" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p042:u013" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p044:u017" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u004.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u013.s001" />
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-024: A MACsec device supports supplicant and authenticator functions across arrangements. EAPRole describes those functions separately from DeviceKind. The AS is bound to one site network in the selected interpretation; one AS must not bridge Red and Gray or several site networks.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-027: The key server is an endpoint function. MACsecServerPair and the actual central-management-site declaration determine the server’s placement. Approved key-generation provenance remains an explicit authority condition, including the chosen EAP-derived CAK interpretation.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-management-component">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
