    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p052:u005" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p052:u006" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p053:u005" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p053:u009" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p053:u011" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p053:u013" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p055:u016" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p056:u010.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p059:u010.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p060:u010.s001" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p061:u007.s001" />
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-015: When built-in encapsulation is unavailable, the selected standalone encapsulator must have the required Inner-side and Outer-side attachments and satisfy its applicable component duties. The current RG-015 definition preserves those duties despite the source passage describing encapsulation as outside the solution boundary.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-supplicant">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:comment>MACsec Device authentication function; each device performs both supplicant and authenticator functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Supplicant</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ExtractedRole" />
    <skos:altLabel>supplicant</skos:altLabel>
    <tdn:associatedRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-024" />
    <tdn:directRequirement rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:RG-024" />
    <tdn:leanExpression>EAPRole.supplicant</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanExpression>MACsecAuthentication.supportedRoles</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanMapping>The EAP role is a protocol function recorded separately from device kind. A MACsec device can support both functions across different arrangements.</tdn:leanMapping>
    <tdn:leanReference>EAPRole at TDN/Requirements/CoreMscRequirements.lean:273</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>MACsecAuthentication at TDN/Requirements/CoreMscRequirements.lean:358</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>msc_macsec_authentication_choice_and_as at TDN/Requirements/MasterMscRequirementSpecs.lean:38</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanRepresentation>direct</tdn:leanRepresentation>
    <tdn:roleId>ROLE-supplicant</tdn:roleId>
    <tdn:roleKind>device_or_service_role</tdn:roleKind>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p026:u006.s002" />
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-024: A MACsec device supports supplicant and authenticator functions across arrangements. EAPRole describes those functions separately from DeviceKind. The AS is bound to one site network in the selected interpretation; one AS must not bridge Red and Gray or several site networks.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-switch">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:comment>Device alternative for standalone encapsulation or Gray infrastructure forwarding; switching as an activity is not an instance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Switch</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ExtractedRole" />
    <skos:altLabel>router/switch</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>switch</skos:altLabel>
    <tdn:leanExpression>Deployment.OrdinaryGray</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanExpression>DeviceKind.ordinaryGraySwitch</tdn:leanExpression>
    <tdn:leanMapping>An ordinary Gray switch has a dedicated kind, no encryption layer and no infrastructure flag. It has at least one Gray interface and only Gray or local interfaces. Other switching behavior is represented through packet-processing records.</tdn:leanMapping>
    <tdn:leanReference>Deployment at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:581</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>Deployment.OrdinaryGray at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:668</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>DeviceKind at TDN/Requirements/MscComplianceSchema.lean:11</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanReference>Zone at TDN/Requirements/TwoLayerOverlayArchitecture.lean:40</tdn:leanReference>
    <tdn:leanRepresentation>context</tdn:leanRepresentation>
    <tdn:roleId>ROLE-switch</tdn:roleId>
    <tdn:roleKind>device_or_service_role</tdn:roleKind>
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p021:u008.s004" />
    <tdn:sourceUnit rdf:resource="urn:tdn:csfc:source:CSFC-MSC-1.3.0-4e40e3d83708:p025:u007.s003" />
    <tdn:theoryInterpretation>V31-056-074: Ordinary Gray routing and switching infrastructure has a narrowly defined exemption from component duties. OrdinaryGray requires the matching kind, no encryption layer or infrastructure flag, at least one Gray interface, and only Gray or local interfaces. Standalone encapsulators retain their applicable duties.</tdn:theoryInterpretation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles:ROLE-testing-equipment">
